WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.607
An AI agent is told: increase our subscription from one hundred to one hundred twenty seats.

2
00:00:05.607 --> 00:00:14.688
Simple, until three things go wrong: a required dependency is missing, the financial consequences are unclear, and the execution itself is uncertain.

3
00:00:14.988 --> 00:00:21.139
The agent proposes the seat increase, but the required analytics entitlement is missing from the change.

4
00:00:21.139 --> 00:00:28.710
MSE evaluates the whole set, read-only, before anything is dispatched, and refuses it, with a witness naming the missing add-on.

5
00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:32.318
Include the add-on, and the complete change passes admission.

6
00:00:32.318 --> 00:00:36.636
Admission is not authorization: it judges completeness, never permission.

7
00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:49.337
Next, SCQ quotes the financial consequences before any mutation: an immediate effect of two hundred dollars, and a resulting recurring amount of twelve hundred dollars, each marked determined, not guessed.

8
00:00:49.337 --> 00:00:54.600
A separate approval policy, the caller's own code, not the protocol, accepts the quote.

9
00:00:54.600 --> 00:01:00.408
The change commits against the simulator, and the receipt records: committed, reconciliation OK.

10
00:01:00.708 --> 00:01:08.457
After a restart, re-executing the same intent does not dispatch again: the durable coordinator replays the recorded receipt.

11
00:01:08.457 --> 00:01:10.332
One dispatch, start to finish.

12
00:01:10.332 --> 00:01:20.580
A lost provider response is a different case: the outcome is indeterminate, retry is refused, and reconciliation happens by observation, never by blind re-dispatch.

13
00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.456
Try Agorail in five minutes.

14
00:01:22.456 --> 00:01:26.566
The packages are on npm, and the quickstart needs no billing credentials.

15
00:01:26.566 --> 00:01:31.632
Agorail is experimental research software: no production billing certification is claimed.
